<div class="hero-copy"><div class="eyebrow">TECHNOLOGY × ECOLOGY × INFRASTRUCTURE × PLACE</div><h1>Ecological intelligence for the technological age.</h1><p class="lead">Exploring the relationships between digital systems, natural environments, physical infrastructure, and the communities that bring them to life.</p><a href="#research" class="pill">EXPLORE OUR WORK <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="hero-side">PEOPLE<br>PLACES<br>SYSTEMS<br>A HEALTHIER<br>TOMORROW<br><br>01 / 04</div></header>
<main><section class="section perspective" id="about"><img class="landscape-large" src="landscape-river.jpg" alt="Illustrated forest valley and winding river" loading="lazy"><div><div class="eyebrow">OUR PERSPECTIVE</div><h2>A more connected view of technology.</h2><p>Every digital system relies on something physical — energy, water, land, infrastructure, and the communities surrounding it. Fieldline Systems explores what becomes visible when we stop separating technology from the environments that make it possible.</p><a class="pill" href="#systems">LEARN MORE <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div><div class="triptych"><img src="landscape-hills.jpg" alt="Green rolling hills" loading="lazy"><img src="landscape-water.jpg" alt="Water winding through a valley" loading="lazy"><img src="landscape-city.jpg" alt="City skyline" loading="lazy"></div><p class="eyebrow">TECHNOLOGY × ECOLOGY<br>INFRASTRUCTURE × PLACE</p></div></section>
